<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The permanent half of the gene, and its only real cost.

       partEfficiencyOffset rather than a capMod: the part the hole lands in is rolled, so this
       mod cannot know in advance whether it is naming manipulation or walking. Stating the loss
       on the part instead lets the engine work out which capacities that part served, which
       stays correct for whatever the roll picked and for animals and modded bodies too. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteHole</defName>
    <label>involute hole</label>
    <labelNoun>an involute hole</labelNoun>
    <description>There is a hole in this part. Not a wound - a hole, with nothing on the other side of it that belongs to this body.\n\nMost of the time it leads nowhere and is simply missing tissue. When the carrier connects it, whatever strikes this part goes through instead of landing.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.62, 0.35, 0.95)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <makesSickThought>false</makesSickThought>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <partEfficiencyOffset>-0.5</partEfficiencyOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <!-- The window in which the hole leads somewhere. Duration lives on the comp rather than on
       a Disappears comp for the same reason every other gene in this mod counts its own: an
       accelerated pawn ticks its hediffs several times per game tick and would close early. -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>AG_InvoluteVented</defName>
    <label>vented</label>
    <description>The hole is connected. Anything that finds the part it is in does not land - it arrives somewhere else, in a room this person can walk to and nobody else can.\n\nWhat goes through is not stopped, slowed or reduced. It is still travelling, and it is still dangerous to whatever is in there.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.62, 0.35, 0.95)</defaultLabelColor>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <makesSickThought>false</makesSickThought>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_DisappearsOnDeath" />
      <li Class="RimArt.HediffCompProperties_Vent">
        <durationTicks>1800</durationTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
